context_info = ()
i = 0
for d in context:
    result = llm_query("You are given a document. Extract facts relevant to the following riddle-like query.\n\nQuery description:\n- We are looking for a male individual outstanding in his field of work, who was awarded a doctorate (PhD) at a university founded in the 18th century (1701–1800).\n- This same individual received advice from a man known as the \"father of a nuclear weapon\" (e.g., Robert Oppenheimer — \"father of the atomic bomb\"; Edward Teller — \"father of the hydrogen bomb\"; Andrei Sakharov — \"father of the Soviet hydrogen bomb\"; Abdul Qadeer Khan — \"father of Pakistan's nuclear bomb\"; Homi J. Bhabha — \"father of the Indian nuclear programme\"; others with similar epithets).\n- He shares a name with a politician in an African country who expressed gratitude toward a late journalist who hosted a political talk show in the 21st century.\n- We need the name of the scientific concept attributed to this individual.\n\nDocument:\nBEGIN\n" + d + "\nEND\n\nFrom ONLY this document, extract any of the following, if present. For each item, give the lines under headers 'Item:' followed by 'Quotes:' (exact relevant snippets) and then 'Details:' present concise details.\n\n1) Scientist/academic who earned a doctorate at a university founded in the 18th century. Include name, field, doctorate institution, institution founding year, and any scientific concept(s), theorem(s), law(s) or effect(s) named after him.\n\n2) Instances where a person is described as receiving advice (advised by, suggestion from, mentored by, supervised by, counsel from) by any of: Robert Oppenheimer, Edward Teller, Andrei Sakharov, Abdul Qadeer Khan, Homi J. Bhabha, Enrico Fermi, Ernest Lawrence. Include who received the advice and the adviser's epithet (e.g., 'father of the atomic bomb').\n\n3) Mentions of an African politician expressing gratitude to a late journalist who hosted a political talk show (name of politician, country, journalist, show, that the journalist is deceased). Include the politician's name exactly as written.\n\n4) Any explicit hint that ties a scientist's name to a politician's name (same first or last name). State both names.\n\nIf the document contains none of the above, say 'No relevant items.'")
    context_info = context_info + ("Doc " + str(i) + " analysis:\n" + result,)
    i = i + 1

join_str = "\n\n".join(context_info)

final = llm_query("Task: Identify the scientific concept attributed to the individual described below, using the extracted items.\n\nDescription:\n- Male, outstanding in his field.\n- Earned a doctorate at a university founded in the 18th century (1701–1800).\n- Received advice from a man known as the 'father of a nuclear weapon' (e.g., Robert Oppenheimer – father of the atomic bomb; Edward Teller – father of the hydrogen bomb; Andrei Sakharov; Abdul Qadeer Khan; Homi J. Bhabha).\n- Shares a name with an African politician who expressed gratitude toward a late journalist who hosted a political talk show in the 21st century.\n\nExtracted items from the documents:\n" + join_str + "\n\nAnswer with ONLY the exact name of the scientific concept attributed to this individual (no explanation).")
return_result(final)